            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Cyndee MacPhee"
            },
            "reviewBody": "The ham is great. I only gave 4 stars simply because I felt one only needed half the ingredients and I felt it best to braise ham in the last 30 - 45 minutes only (personal choice). I also used cloves all over ham at the outset. But wonderful taste and a definite keeper. Thanks so much :)",
            "datePublished": "2015-08-10T07:04:11.613Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Sylvia Longenecker Weaver"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Excellent glaze for our Easter boneless ham. Since we are older and watch how much sugar we use, I cut the amount of brown sugar down to one cup. I added 1/2 t. ground cloves, and instead of using pineapple rings, I used a small can of crushed pineapple. Because the syrup was thick enough, the pineapple remained coated over the entire ham, rather than running off as many glazes do. This recipe resulted in a beautiful appearance and delicious taste. This is a keeper!",
            "datePublished": "2018-04-06T12:23:00.680Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "CCS"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I needed to add more than double the quantity of mustard to make a sauce -- next time I'll start with less brown sugar. Used fresh pineapple rings instead of canned but the recommended amount of pineapple juice was an essential ingredient for basting. I'll never use the packaged glaze again -- this made an absolutely delicious ham.",
            "datePublished": "2017-04-17T22:56:22.770Z"
