              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Randy"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I made this recipe exactly as written. All the ingredients and measures were as written. I put a 10 lb bone in half ham in an 18 qt nesco on a rack. I poured all ingredients listed in order over the ham. Set the nesco at 325. Roasted it for 3 to 3 1/2 hours. I inserted a meat thermometer, when it reached 135 degrees, it was done. This was the best tasting, and moistess ham I have ever made. I will make my ham this way going forward.",
